import DocsLayout from '../layouts/DocsLayout.astro';
---
<DocsLayout title="Roadmap">
  <h1>Roadmap</h1>
  <p>A living, lightweight view of where Fate's Edge is headed — not a promise of dates. The authoritative, granular backlog lives in each repo's issue tracker; this page is the "why would I care" summary for new contributors.</p>

  <h2>Now</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Stabilizing the Tag DSL surface so third-party GM directives don't break on upgrade.</li>
    <li>Expanding transport-layer event parity across all client surfaces.</li>
    <li>Growing the LLM driver roster beyond the current defaults.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Next</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>A mobile-friendly client surface.</li>
    <li>More adventure modules from the community, using the JSON-based, rules-native format.</li>
    <li>Voice stack adapters beyond the current TTS/RVC pipeline.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Later / exploratory</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Additional VTT integrations beyond Roll20 and Foundry.</li>
    <li>Community-run adventure module registry.</li>
  </ul>

  <p>Want to influence this list? Open an issue on the relevant repo, or raise it in <a href="https://github.com/Chronophage-net/fate-edge-dev/discussions">Discussions</a> — roadmap items generally start there before they're formalized.</p>
</DocsLayout>
